  "oral_argument": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a200b9513b155c317e08c8a4124eca890154c0546a09259fe88aeb932b7f9c02",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a200b9513b15-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 5,
              "start": 5
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, do the police need a separate warrant to retrieve the car for which they already have a warrant?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a200b9513b155c317e08c8a4124eca890154c0546a09259fe88aeb932b7f9c02",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a200b9513b15-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito, does the search fall within or outside the curtilage, and does that determine whether the Fourth Amendment applies?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a200b9513b155c317e08c8a4124eca890154c0546a09259fe88aeb932b7f9c02",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a200b9513b15-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 23,
              "start": 23
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito, do you dispute that the police had probable cause to believe the tarp-covered item was the motorcycle they were looking for?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a200b9513b155c317e08c8a4124eca890154c0546a09259fe88aeb932b7f9c02",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a200b9513b15-0001-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 24,
              "start": 24
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, do you agree that the policeman on the sidewalk knew, or at least had probable cause to know, that the tarp-covered item was the possibly stolen motorcycle?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Alito",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a200b9513b155c317e08c8a4124eca890154c0546a09259fe88aeb932b7f9c02",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a200b9513b15-0001-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 30,
              "start": 30
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Alito, did you admit that the police had probable cause to believe the tarp-covered thing was the motorcycle they had been chasing?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a200b9513b155c317e08c8a4124eca890154c0546a09259fe88aeb932b7f9c02",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a200b9513b15-0001-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 39,
              "start": 39
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Breyer, is the law that a policeman cannot enter a house until he gets a warrant, even when he sees the stolen item through a window?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a200b9513b155c317e08c8a4124eca890154c0546a09259fe88aeb932b7f9c02",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a200b9513b15-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 46,
              "start": 46
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Sotomayor, is the difference between opening a garage door and simply walking into a car de minimis?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a200b9513b155c317e08c8a4124eca890154c0546a09259fe88aeb932b7f9c02",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a200b9513b15-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 47,
              "start": 47
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Gorsuch, does the automobile exception trace back to the original Carroll decision, which analogized cars to ships in 1790?"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "a200b9513b155c317e08c8a4124eca890154c0546a09259fe88aeb932b7f9c02",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-a200b9513b15-0002-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 61,
              "start": 61
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Kagan, was there one search here or were there two searches?"
      }
    ],
